    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The medical residency is a unique time in the life of a resident (doctor-in-training). A resident’s role oscillates in a quantum state between “employee” and “learner” as they are tasked to simultaneously care for real patients during rounds while they learn in situ. Resident’s experiences during clinical rounds are the bedrock of their learning: As University of Wisconsin School of Medicine professor Dr. HB Slotnick writes, “both the experiences and the insights extracted from them become the corpus to which [residents] will refer when seeking to understand and resolve problems in the future” (Slotnick, 2001). \r\n\r\nWhile the immersive, experiential element of rounding is a given, the “extraction of insights” is more complicated in practice. Residents are not tasked to reflect on their rounding experiences, nor are they provided tools/frameworks with which to do so (Nothnagle, Goldman, Quirk, & Reis, 2010). Residents struggle to identify their own strengths and weaknesses and are not incentivized to craft self-directed learning goals. Simultaneously, faculty attendings (training doctors) do not provide specific, targeted feedback to residents. These factors hinder residents’ potential for learning and growth during one of the most crucial chapters of their education as future doctors.\r\n\r\nRound Up! seeks to challenge these phenomena by helping residents learn how to become self-reflective learners during their residency. Round Up! is an app-based intervention that provides tools to help residents reflect on their experiences, define learning goals, and seek targeted feedback from attendings. Ultimately, the objective is to support doctors not only as experts in their profession, but also, as learners with a mindset towards continuous growth.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
